# Root-only Restic backup configuration.
#
# Provisioning copies this file to /srv/peptides/backup.env as root:root mode
# 0600. Values are parsed as plain data: no quotes, expansion or shell syntax.
#
# BACKUP_REPOSITORY_FILE contains the Restic repository string, for example:
#   sftp:backup@example.net:/srv/restic/peptides
#   s3:https://object.example.net/peptides
# It and BACKUP_PASSWORD_FILE remain root-owned, mode 0600 and nonempty. For
# each run, backup.sh makes short-lived root:peptides-backup 0640 copies inside
# its private state directory. Every Restic/network command runs through
# setpriv as that non-login UID with empty supplementary groups/capabilities
# and an allowlisted environment; the copies are revoked and removed afterward.
# The BACKUP_* names become explicit Restic CLI flags and inherited RESTIC_*
# controls never reach the restricted child.
BACKUP_REPOSITORY_FILE=/srv/peptides/restic-repository
BACKUP_PASSWORD_FILE=/srv/peptides/restic-password

# Retention is enforced after every successful snapshot.
BACKUP_KEEP_DAILY=7
BACKUP_KEEP_WEEKLY=5
BACKUP_KEEP_MONTHLY=12

# Optional percentage of repository data read by each check. Leave blank for
# metadata/structure checks only; use a value from 1% through 100% to sample
# stored pack data as well.
BACKUP_CHECK_READ_DATA_SUBSET=

# Coherent snapshots require both PostgreSQL and the upload tree to be stable.
# The scheduled service stops and proves Medusa inactive only while it creates
# and validates local artifacts, then restarts and health-checks Medusa before
# the slower encrypted off-host transfer. Caddy and the basic-auth preview gate
# remain active throughout; the API is briefly unavailable during staging.
# backup.sh fails closed if this is missing/blank (default 1) and rejects 0.
BACKUP_REQUIRE_STOPPED=1
